<title>USA: Faulding unit gets generic herpes drug OK.</title>
<headline>Faulding unit gets generic herpes drug OK.</headline>
<dateline>ELIZABETH, N.J. 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Faulding Inc said on Friday that its Purepac Pharmaceutical Co unit has received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market acyclovir tablets, an antiviral drug to treat herpes.</p>
<p>The acyclovir tablets are the generic version of Zovirax, marketed by Glaxo Wellcome Plc.</p>
<p>Faulding said that Purepac plans a prompt commercial launch of the product.</p>
<p>It said brand sales were about $240 million in 1996.</p>
</text>
